/Title (The experiment demonstrated how permissions, roles, role hierarchy and data sharing together form a role-based access control mechanism in Zoho Creator. Structured forms and a role-aware dashboard replace the physical register and verbal requests of a manual library counter with clean, consistent, and analysable data. The two-level hierarchy and the directional Read/Write share rule keep information channels controlled: the library admin gains exactly the access needed to review and process student book issue requests, while the CEO retains overall oversight and the student, Faculty, and Staff roles continue to)
